  "worked_solution": "Dividing $88$ by $9$ using integer division, we notice that\n\n$$\n9<88÷9<10.\n$$\n\nThe quotient $q$ is the left-hand value. So $q=9.$\n\nNext, we find the remainder $r$ by computing $r=a-qn.$ This gives\n\n$$\nr=88-(9)(9)=7.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write $88=qn+r$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}88={{9}_{⏟}}_{q}\\cdot 9+{{7}_{⏟}}_{r}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $q\\cdot r=9\\cdot 7=63.$",
